WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Dragon now owns every US record for fastest trips to the ISS after crew 13 docked in 7 hours 55 minutes. This is SpaceX Daily, episode 122. Crew Dragon Grace lifted off from Space Launch Complex 40 and docked to the forward port of the Harmony Module 7 hours and 55 minutes later. That time beat the prior US record by more than 4 hours. The uncrewed CRS-31 cargo flight had held

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:32.540
the previous mark at a little over 12 hours.

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:37.800
Crew 11 had been the fastest crew trip at 14 hours and 43 minutes.

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:45.620
Axiom's Ax2 mission sits fourth at 15 hours and 35 minutes, and NASA's crew 4 is fifth

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:47.780
at 15 hours and 44 minutes.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:50.060
All five flights use Dragon.

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:56.980
SpaceX's Juliana Shimon said the station happened to be in an opportune spot in its orbit, allowing

00:00:56.980 --> 00:01:02.540
the approach to begin almost immediately after reaching orbit. The timing depends on launch date,

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:08.900
so future flights will not reliably match the result. SpaceX subsidiary Coastal Connect Services

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:14.940
asked the Florida Public Service Commission to approve a tariff for a new 16-inch transmission pipeline.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:21.680
The line would connect SpaceX facilities in Brevard County to the existing Florida Gas Transmission

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:27.440
interstate network. Company filing state that truck deliveries and local pipelines can no longer

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:33.740
meet growing fuel demand for Starship operations at Cape Canaveral. Natural gas would supply methane

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:38.640
feedstock for Raptor engines that burned sub-cooled liquid methane and liquid oxygen.

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:45.380
The project would replace tanker truck deliveries with direct pipeline supply. Space X is already

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:51.940
pursuing a similar eight-mile pipeline near Starbase in Texas. The four-member crew 12 crew will

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:58.920
close the hatch on Dragon Freedom at 6.20 a.m. Eastern Daylight Time on October 7. Undocking from

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:04.040
the forward port of the Harmony Module is scheduled for 8.05 a.m. Eastern Daylight Time.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:10.660
Splashdown off California is planned for 11.34 a.m. Eastern Daylight Time on October 8.

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:17.580
Live coverage of Hatch Closure begins at 6 a.m. Eastern Daylight Time on NASA Plus and agency channels.

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:25.280
Undocking coverage starts at 7.45 a.m. Eastern Daylight Time and switches to audio only after separation.

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:31.980
Deorbit Burn coverage resumes at 10.20 a.m. Eastern Daylight Time on October 8th.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:40.160
The purchases totaled $16.6 million across ARKK, ARKQ, and ARKX funds.

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:46.900
ARK analysts set a US launch bottleneck could emerge if SpaceX retires Falcon 9 by the end

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:47.500
of the decade.

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:53.800
They noted that Falcon 9 is fully booked until 2028 or 2029 for some customers.

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:59.940
ARK sees an enormous opportunity for Rocket Lab and Stokespace if their medium-lift vehicles

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:00.340
deliver.

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:06.800
However, the analysis followed Starship Flight 14, which deployed 26 Starlink V3 satellites

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:08.620
despite an engine shutdown.

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:14.520
The stock reached 171.09, its highest level since mid-June.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:19.940
The gain returned Elon Musk to Trillionaire status according to Forbes' real-time billionaires

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:20.320
list.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:25.900
Shares added nearly 1% in after-hours trading after the Florida pipeline filing.

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:31.220
Sequoia Capital Partner, Sean McGuire, said investors are seeing the very beginning of

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:37.400
understanding SpaceX. Morgan Stanley, analyst Adam Jonas noted that none of 40 clients he

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:47.420
pulled owned SPCX shares. Of those, 11,156 remain in orbit and 11,142 are operational.

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:54.280
Figures come from the October 2, 2026 update. Starlink satellites appear on eight of the

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:57.860
upcoming high-probability conjunction events tracked by SOCRATES,

00:03:58.360 --> 00:04:02.960
non-rated high-risk, 10 star-linked satellites currently have active reentry

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:08.220
predictions, most of them planned deorbitz. The mission launched February 13,

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:13.380
aboard a Falcon 9. The crew supported studies on pneumonia-causing bacteria and

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:18.000
plant microbe interactions in microgravity. Dragon freedom will perform a

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:23.200
deorbit burn at 10.46 am Eastern daylight time on October 8th

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:25.700
before descending under parachutes into the Pacific.

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:28.900
Recovery teams will conduct routine medical checks

00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:30.040
after splashdown.

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:33.580
The mission carried NASA astronauts Jessica Watkins

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:36.900
and Luke Delaney, Canadian Space Agency astronaut

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:40.100
Joshua Kutrick and Ross Cosmos Cosmonaut

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:41.680
Sergei Teteriatnikov.

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:44.240
Dragon arrived nearly an hour ahead

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:47.120
of the projected 8 p.m. Eastern time docking time.

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:50.000
Shimon noted that the faster trip resulted

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:56.140
from orbital geometry rather than hardware changes. Boom's supersonic CEO Blake Scholl criticized

00:04:56.140 --> 00:05:01.500
the regulatory process for the Florida pipeline, writing that bureaucratic permission should not

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:06.960
be required to build in the land of the free. He called for clear, simple, and reasonable rules

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:13.540
enforced only when broken. ARC Invest chief futurist Brett Winton stated that each starship launch

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:19.420
could drive more than $700 million in incremental annual revenue when combined with starling

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:24.600
capacity. He added that monetizing AI software on the satellite network could

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:29.580
increase that figure further. SpaceX has begun hiring natural gas traders to

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:33.680
secure fuel supplies for Starship operations in both Florida and Texas.

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:38.980
Sequoia's McGuire responded to a post noting that few investors appear to own

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:43.780
SPCX, saying the complexity of the business is both a challenge and an

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:48.420
opportunity. One thing worth watching is that the Florida pipeline still requires

00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:51.460
state regulatory approval before construction can begin.

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:57.040
The filing asks the public service commission to set a tariff for the new line, and any

00:05:57.040 --> 00:06:01.820
delay in that process would keep SpaceX reliant on truck deliveries for methane feedstock.

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:06.060
SpaceX has not yet received a response to the September filing.

00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:13.180
On the AI front, ARC estimates that Starship Flight 14's deployment of 26 Starlink V3 satellites

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:17.860
could support nearly $560 million in annualized revenue.

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:22.020
The firm sees full reusability potentially lowering launch costs

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:25.140
to $100 per kilogram or less at scale,

00:06:25.540 --> 00:06:28.100
which would improve orbital data center economics.

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:32.480
ARC also projects SpaceX's 2030 enterprise value

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:37.460
between $1.7 and $3.1 trillion, depending on the scenario.

00:06:38.140 --> 00:06:39.520
From an engineering standpoint,

00:06:39.860 --> 00:06:41.420
the record drag and docking shows

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:46.140
how orbital mechanics can be leveraged when the launch window aligns the vehicle with the

00:06:46.140 --> 00:06:52.120
station's position. Dragon reached orbit and began closing the range almost immediately because the

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:57.840
station was already near the right phasing angle. That geometry removed the need from multiple days

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:03.320
of phasing burns that most missions still perform with the Draco thrusters. The approach trades

00:07:03.320 --> 00:07:09.120
schedule flexibility for speed. Future flights will need the full series of burns unless the station

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:14.260
happens to be in a similar spot. The same principle applies to any rendezvous where the

00:07:14.260 --> 00:07:19.800
chaser starts with a favorable relative position of actor. Reducing the number of burns also lowers

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:24.960
propellant consumption on the vehicle that must later return to Earth. Over many missions,

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:30.740
the cumulative savings in fuel and ground support pine become meaningful, even if each individual

00:07:30.740 --> 00:07:37.720
flight cannot repeat the 7-hour 55-minute mark. A quick look at the tape shows SPCX finished

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:39.540
higher after a strong session.

00:07:40.420 --> 00:07:44.340
Before we go, watch for the next update on whether the Florida Pipeline Terra

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:45.360
receives approval.

